        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the FitShow app?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              FitShow is a free indoor training app for walking, running, cycling and rowing, made by FitShow (Xiamen) Information Technology Co., Ltd. Its Google Play description says it works with treadmills, bikes, ellipticals and rowers, can adjust equipment settings to match your training and routes, and has a library of geolocated route videos. The same company supplies the connection platform built into many budget treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is FitShow free?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              FitShow is free to download. Its Google Play listing on 27 November 2026 said it contains in-app purchases priced from $0.99 to $59.99 per item, but did not say which features are paid. Check the store page on your phone for the current options.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the best treadmill with FitShow?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For most people, the JAGJOG Foldable Treadmill with 15% Auto Incline: up to 8.8 mph, 300 lb, and a listing that names FitShow for tracking and virtual routes, at about $297 on Amazon on 27 November 2026. For running, the Aeriflo X-T510A at about $627, with 12 mph and a 20% incline.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I know if a treadmill works with FitShow?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Read the listing&rsquo;s bullet points and the manual, not just the title. Most treadmills that use FitShow mention it once, in a bullet about Bluetooth or the app. If a listing only says &ldquo;smart app&rdquo;, ask the seller which app it is, because many brands ship their own.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can FitShow control my treadmill’s incline?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              FitShow says it can adjust equipment settings, but only a treadmill with powered incline that accepts the command can follow. A manual-incline treadmill such as the Ksports Advanced Rehab cannot be tilted by any app. None of the listings here states outright that FitShow will raise the deck, so confirm with the seller if it matters.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do FitShow treadmills work with Kinomap or Zwift?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Some do. Of the seven picks, the Aeriflo X-T510A and both Ksports treadmills also name Kinomap, and the two Ksports also name Zwift. The others name FitShow only. Close FitShow before opening another app, because a treadmill usually accepts one connection at a time.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

